  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e7bfb9d3-e64c-4b82-928e-55e473a07ff2-9896038.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 134px;\" /></p><p>Here, the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;act as the reducing agent, as the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi></math>&nbsp;has +1 oxidation state of in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOCl</mi></math>&nbsp;and after reaction with the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, in the presence of the acid, it reduces the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOCl</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;having -1 oxidation state.</p><p>So, as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi></math>&nbsp;oxidation state decreases from the +1 to -1 oxidation state, hence the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is acting as the reducing agent.</p>",
